cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  To cite a single fact, cite the claim: its page at https://blocklore.space/claims/ID shows each
  revision and its sources. To cite Blocklore as a whole, use this entry.
title: Blocklore
abstract: >-
  A public library of Bitcoin facts that checks itself. Every sentence is a claim with its sources
  and an exact quote that code finds at the link before it publishes, code is cited at a commit,
  every change is kept as a revision, and each edition is sealed in a Bitcoin block.
type: software
authors:
  - alias: Xaxis
url: https://blocklore.space
repository-code: https://github.com/Xaxis/blocklore.space
license:
  - MIT
  - CC-BY-4.0
keywords:
  - bitcoin
  - education
  - knowledge base
  - verifiable
  - citations
  - opentimestamps
  - mcp
